From 0b60bb611c012fc5da1f0d4b439a803dfa193870 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:27:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: dt-bindings: qcom: Describe an APC-aware PM8226
 boot hold

The live CPU APC rail can outlast bootloader handoff while Pronto requests
its own lower MX floor before CPR attaches. Describe an optional boot APC
supply for the paired PM8226 L3 voters so the provider can validate the
inherited rail and establish a temporary maximum MX vote before either
voter is registered.

The CPU consumer hands off with an enabled AO request covering the rounded
boot APC voltage and must retain that request while APC can remain live.
The temporary vote contributes only to ACTIVE. Require explicit AO voltage
bounds and exclude automatic boot-on/always-on enables from this handoff.
Existing unguarded voters retain their previous meaning.

Codex generated this change and its host qualification. Human review and
DCO certification remain pending. No maintainer contact or publication.

Backport this prerequisite to maintained Linux 6.18.63. The complete
seventeen-change batch passes native ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT object
builds with the MSM8926 feature enabled and disabled. CPU-idle is ARM
only. Host fault models use synthetic services and normal LeakSanitizer;
firmware, electrical and physical suspend acceptance remain open.

Codex prepared this local backport and verification. Original authors,
dates, licenses and human attribution tags are retained. Human DCO and
review remain pending. No phone access or publication occurred.

Backported from commit 6c9b8b686ea5 ("regulator: dt-bindings: qcom:
Describe an APC-aware PM8226 boot hold")
---
 .../regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml     | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml
index 8c68c3cdbe35e..8aec6aba3a868 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml
@@ -123,6 +123,17 @@ properties:
       regulator-state-standby: false
     unevaluatedProperties: false
 
+  qcom,boot-apc-supply:
+    description:
+      Live CPU APC supply whose boot voltage must be covered before the paired
+      PM8226 L3 voters can change the active MX request. Before registering
+      either voter, read and validate APC against l3-ao's voltage range. Hold
+      the l3-ao maximum as a temporary active enable and voltage request until
+      an enabled l3-ao request covers the rounded-up boot APC voltage. The CPU
+      consumer must establish and retain that covering request before changing
+      APC. This boot hold does not contribute to the sleep set. l3-ao must not
+      be enabled by boot-on or always-on constraints before consumer handoff.
+
 patternProperties:
   ".*-supply$":
     description: Input supply phandle(s) for this node
@@ -145,6 +156,23 @@ allOf:
     else:
       properties:
         l3-ao: false
+  - if:
+      required:
+        - qcom,boot-apc-supply
+    then:
+      required:
+        - l3
+        - l3-ao
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          const: qcom,rpm-pm8226-regulators
+        l3-ao:
+          required:
+            - regulator-min-microvolt
+            - regulator-max-microvolt
+          properties:
+            regulator-boot-on: false
+            regulator-always-on: false
 
 required:
   - compatible
